  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 202 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nNearby surface ridging and southerly surface flow will keep \ntemperatures hot over the weekend. Upper 90s to lower 100s appear \nlikely with some risk of reaching heat advisory criteria across \nparts of southern Oklahoma and north Texas (particularly on \nSaturday).\n\nBeing on the edge of the upper high, we will maintain at least \nlow PoPs, particularly in northern and eastern Oklahoma. \nDeterministic models have shown consistency in depicting an MCS \nSaturday night, though its currently forecast trajectory would \nmainly impact eastern Oklahoma.\n\nHigh confidence in hot temperatures and low rain chances now\nextends through Monday afternoon. After this, confidence drops off\ndramatically with the possible arrival of a cold front sometime\nearly to mid week next week. Models vary greatly in timing and\nstrength of the front. Continued hot and dry weather remains the\nmore likely scenario (70-80%), though the outlier solutions would\nbring substantial cooling.\n\nDay",
